<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28272" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Māzăces</span></b> , um,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A people of Numidia</i>, afterwards called
			Mazacenses: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mazacum turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 30</span></i>
			.—In <i>sing. collect.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mazax</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Luc. 4,
			681</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Stil. 1,
			356</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A people near the Palus Mæotis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 7,
				6, § 21</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
